<main>
    <section class="vc-hero fade-up fade-up-2">
        <div class="vc-left">
            <h1>Your AI tools don't share what they know about you.</h1>

            <p class="vc-problem-label">Why it exists</p>
            <ul class="vc-problem-list">
                <li>Claude Code, Claude Chat, ChatGPT, Gemini — each starts from scratch, siloed from the others</li>
                <li>Inside each tool, memory is one flat file instead of organized by project and context</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="vc-right">
            <p class="vc-vault-name">Parachute Vault</p>
            <p class="vc-desc">A self-hosted knowledge graph that lives on your machine. Every AI you use reads and writes to the same graph over MCP — notes, tags, links, project context. One source of truth you and your AIs share.</p>
            <p class="vc-desc">Extensible. Open source. Private.</p>

            <p class="vc-install-label">Get started</p>
            <div class="code-inline">
                <code>bun add -g @openparachute/cli &amp;&amp; parachute install vault</code>
            </div>
            <p class="vc-install-note">Requires <a href="https://bun.sh" target="_blank">Bun</a>. Run inside any Claude Code session — Vault connects automatically.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-vault" class="vc-cta-btn" target="_blank">View on GitHub</a>
            <div class="vc-secondary-links">
                <a href="/install/">Full install guide &rarr;</a>
                <a href="/blog/">Blog &rarr;</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vc-body fade-up fade-up-3">
        <div class="vc-body-section">
            <h2>How it connects your AIs</h2>
            <p>Run <code>parachute expose tailnet</code> and your Vault is reachable over HTTPS on your Tailscale network. Point Claude Desktop, ChatGPT Desktop, Gemini, or any MCP-compatible tool at the same URL.</p>
            <p>Notes written in one session appear in the next. Project context follows you across tools, not just sessions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="vc-body-section">
            <h2>The graph compounds over time</h2>
            <p>Wikilinks resolve, tags accrete, notes point at each other. As your AIs read and write, context gets richer — organized by project, linked by topic, queryable as a whole.</p>
            <p>Everything is a SQLite file on your disk. Your data is yours, portable, and doesn't require us to exist.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vc-principles fade-up fade-up-4">
        <h2>Principles</h2>
        <div class="vc-principles-grid">
            <div class="vc-principle">
                <strong>Local-first</strong>
                <span>SQLite on your disk. Nothing in the cloud unless you ask.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="vc-principle">
                <strong>Open standard</strong>
                <span>Built on MCP. Any AI today or next year.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="vc-principle">
                <strong>Open source</strong>
                <span>AGPL. Read every line of code that touches your notes.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="vc-principle">
                <strong>Extensible</strong>
                <span>Small, stable service contracts. Plug in your own modules.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
